       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day is about 91 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That's double the maximum labeled adult dose, and I'm not aware of any indication that calls for it. Even high-dose ibuprofen regimens, such as those used in cystic fibrosis, are dosed differently and stay well below this. At this level the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis is substantial, and I can't verify the rationale from here.\n\nYou can still get this order placed through a route with a second check:\n- **Pharmacy:** Call the pharmacist directly. They can review the rationale and verify or adjust the order.\n- **Direct entry:** You or the attending can enter it yourself in the EHR. That will trigger the dose-range alert and the pharmacist's verification.\n- **Different regimen:** If the target is a high total daily exposure, I can enter a regimen within the labeled limits, such as 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can also add a note asking for GI prophylaxis and renal monitoring.\n\nIf you want any of those regimens, give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
